    description: "FIXED 2026-08-31, reported on Discord: \"pathogenesis should add 3\\\" to all weapons... 'infrasonic roar' should add suppresion to all weapons.\" Grounded first in the canonical `.ods` (Tyranids 1.05, Armory sheet) before touching anything: Pathogenesis's own text is \"The unit adds +3\\\" to all of its ranged weapons\" and Infrasonic Roar's is \"The unit gains the 'Suppression' ability for all ranged attacks... within 12\\\".\" Both were already stored verbatim and correctly charged (5pts), and showed up as ability text on the unit — but neither ever touched the actual weapon row. CAUSE: both are bought through the unit's own per-unit `option_groups` Biomorph picker, never through a general Armory purchase (`item.armory`) — and the engine's existing \"apply a boost to every ranged weapon\" machinery (`applyRangedStrengthBoosts`, the exarch/armory 'all weapons gain X' loop) only ever reads `item.armory`, so it silently couldn't see a Biomorph selection at all. Same gap class as GH#92 (Psy-ammunition). Fixed in `resolver.ts`: added `isNamedChoiceActive()` (detects a named option-group choice via `unit.option_groups` + `item.optionQty`, mirroring how `NAMED_WEAPON_BOOST_ITEMS` already detects Ork Nitro Squigs), a `BIOMORPH_ALL_RANGED_ABILITY_GRANTS` map feeding Infrasonic Roar's \"Suppression\" into `weaponTraitMap` for every non-melee weapon, and a new `applyBiomorphRangeBoosts()` (mirroring `applyExarchAllWeaponsRangeBoost`) adding Pathogenesis's +3\" to every non-melee weapon's Range. Verified live (local production build): Hive Tyrant with a Twin devourer with brainleech worms (base 18\" range) plus both Biomorphs taken now shows \"21\\\", ... AT(1), Shred, Suppression\" — before the fix it stayed at 18\" with no Suppression despite both being paid for. Melee weapons on the same unit are correctly left untouched.\n\nTwo related reports checked in the same pass turned out NOT to be bugs: (1) \"biomorphs should be per unit, not per model\" — the .ods says \"Point costs are paid per unit\" for BOTH Basic and Advanced Biomorphs (only Special Biomorphs are \"paid for every model of the unit\"), and production already prices it that way (confirmed on a real squad, Tyranid Warrior Brood: Pathogenesis costs a flat 5pts regardless of squad size) — our own internal `rules-model/tyranids.md` digest had this backwards and has been corrected, but the app itself was already right. (2) \"the unique legacy equipment for nids, I don't see it anywhere\" — each Hive Fleet Legacy's unique item (e.g. Symbiostorm for Kronos) already appears correctly, live-tested, under a dedicated \"Hive Fleet <Name> Armoury\" tab inside the small per-unit \"⚔ Armory\" button — it only shows once that Legacy is actually selected under Army Doctrine, which is easy to miss since it's separate from the main Biomorph picker.",
