    description: "FIXED 2026-09-02, found while building a player's own Chaos Space Marines army list (a Chosen bought \"Daemonic armor\" — \"The model gains a 2+ save\" — and the live profile's SV column never changed). CAUSE: the shared equipment-mod parser (`equipMods.ts`) that turns an item's plain-English description into an actual stat change only recognized an armor-save grant when the text repeated the word \"armor\"/\"armour\" immediately before \"save\" (`/(\\d)\\+\\s+armou?r\\s+save/i`, matching \"2+ armor save\"). All 12 affected items instead read the bare \"The model gains a 2+ save\" with no \"armor\"/\"armour\" word anywhere near \"save\" (the word only appears in the item's NAME, not its rules text) — so the regex never matched, `armorSave` stayed null, and the purchase silently did nothing except take the player's points. Grepped every faction's Armory for the same bare phrasing to find the full list: Chaos Space Marines' Daemonic armor, Chaos Daemons' Hellfire armor, Dark Eldar's Executioner's armour, Eldar's Heavy armor plating and Vaul's cuirass, Grey Knights' and Inquisition's Master-crafted armor, Inquisition's Plate armour/Power amor/Carapace armour, Leagues of Votann's Forgewrought armor, and Tau Empire's Master-crafted suit. One near-match was deliberately left alone: Tau's Earth caste pilot array (\"a 4+ save against losing a wound from Overheating\") is a narrower, conditional mechanic, not a general armor-save upgrade — the fix excludes any \"gains a X+ save\" phrase immediately followed by \"against\" so this one still resolves as descriptive text rather than a real save change. Verified live: Argel Tal (a Chosen with Daemonic armor bought) now shows a 2+ save instead of the base 3+.",
