    description: "FIXED 2026-08-29 (GitHub #107: \"swapping both monstrous scything talons for lash whips and bone swords on a hive tyrant doesn't change the weapon name to 2x lash whip and bonesword\"). CAUSE: `resolver.ts`'s per-weapon quantity computation splits a combo choice name on \"&\"/\"and\" so a genuine multi-weapon grant (\"Chainsword & Laspistol\") counts as two separate weapons. That same split fires on a SINGLE weapon whose own name happens to contain the word \"and\" — \"Lash whip and bonesword\" splits into \"Lash whip\"/\"bonesword\", neither of which matches any real weapon row, so the granted quantity was never recorded at all. The weapon still SHOWED (a separate, earlier visibility pass already tries the full choice name as a fallback candidate — this exact wording is in its own code comment, \"Shardnet and impaler\" included), it just never got COUNTED, so buying it twice (a Hive Tyrant swapping BOTH Monstrous scything talons for it, one per independent swap group) displayed a single unprefixed row as if only one had been bought. Fixed by adding the same \"try the full name too\" fallback to the quantity-counting pass that the visibility pass already had — a genuine combo choice's full name has no matching single weapon row, so this is a no-op for that case, verified by re-testing Adeptus Custodes' Galatus Contemptor Dreadnought's \"Achillus dreadspear & 2 Infernus incinerators\" combo swap (still correctly grants both weapons with the right per-arm counts). Also affects Tyranid Warrior Brood and Tyrant Guard Brood (same \"Lash whip and Bonesword\" choice, per-model stepper instead of Hive Tyrant's two independent one-of-N groups) and potentially Dark Eldar's Wyches/Hekatrix Bloodbrides (\"Shardnet and impaler\") — not individually re-tested, but the same code path. Verified live: a Hive Tyrant with both Monstrous scything talons swapped to Lash whip and bonesword now shows \"2x Lash whip and bonesword\"; swapping to two DIFFERENT weapons instead (Twin devourer with brainleech worms + Lash whip and bonesword) correctly shows \"1x\" of each, not merged or doubled.",
