    description: "FIXED 2026-08-29 (Rigzar: \"primero repara todo\"). Found while fixing GitHub #106 (Telemon Heavy Dreadnought) — the Galatus Contemptor Dreadnought's second Armory option group is worded identically (\"Can swap each Infernus incinerator\") and was ALSO stuck on a single exclusive pick instead of one swap per copy. Unlike the Telemon, its 2 Infernus incinerators are not part of the base loadout at all (`equipped_with` only lists \"Galatus shield; Galatus warblade\"); they only exist if the player picks a DIFFERENT, earlier option group's single choice (\"Achillus dreadspear & 2 Infernus incinerators\") — so the fix needed two things the Telemon didn't. FIX: (1) added `requires_choice: [\"Achillus dreadspear & 2 Infernus incinerators\"]` to the swap group (the same field/mechanism already used for the Space Marine Dreadnought's Storm bolter swap) — the group is now correctly hidden until that arm is actually taken, instead of being selectable with zero Infernus incinerators on the model. (2) `weaponCopiesPerModel()` (equipMods.ts) gained an optional fallback source: when a weapon's copy count isn't found in `equipped_with`, it now also checks the names of any choices the swap's own `requires_choice` points at — \"Achillus dreadspear & 2 Infernus incinerators\" states its own \"2\", which is exactly what the per-arm-swap math needs. Also changed `constraint.type` \"one\" → \"every\" on the swap group itself, mirroring the Telemon fix. Verified live: before buying the Achillus dreadspear option, the swap group is correctly hidden entirely; after buying it, \"Can swap each Infernus incinerator\" shows 2 independent quantity steppers, and swapping each to a different weapon (Lastrum storm bolter + Twin adrathic destructor) correctly replaces both with no leftover Infernus incinerator, totalling 237 + 13 + 19 + 22 = 291pts.",
