    description: "FIXED 2026-08-29, GitHub #106 (\"you can only select one weapon to swap to, and it only swaps one melee arm to ranged... I should be able to swap each arm individually for either ranged weapon\"). CAUSE, two parts. (1) The Telemon's own datasheet header reads \"Can swap EACH Telemon caestus with Twin plasma projector\" (it carries 2 of that combo arm) — the same wording the app already has a working pattern for elsewhere (Eldar War Walker's twin Scatter lasers, GitHub #81: a per-copy swap using `constraint: { type: 'every' }` so each copy gets its own independent pick), but the Telemon's option group was data-entered as `constraint: { type: 'one' }`, an exclusive single pick with no quantity stepper at all — so only one swap could ever be made, for the whole unit, no matter how the header read. (2) Even fixing #1 alone would not have hidden the old weapons correctly: the resolver reads a swap's \"how many copies until this weapon fully disappears from the profile\" threshold from a per-WEAPON-NAME count in the datasheet text, evaluated independently for each name the swap replaces — \"2 Telemon caestus\" gives caestus a count of 2, but \"with Twin plasma projector\" never repeats a number of its own (it's a single combo swap, so the projector's copy count is only implied by the caestus's), so the projector was defaulting to a threshold of 1 and would vanish after only ONE arm swapped instead of two, stranding a caestus without its paired projector on the display. FIX: (1) the option group's constraint is now `'every'`, matching the War Walker precedent — the swap now offers 2 independent picks, matching the \"each\" wording; each pick can be a different weapon (Arachnus storm cannon on one arm, Iliastus accelerator culverin on the other). (2) the resolver's disappear-threshold check now recognizes a per-copy \"each\" swap at the GROUP level (any weapon it replaces counts, not just the one the header's \"each\" sits next to), so every weapon in a combo swap uses the SAME threshold instead of the paired weapon silently defaulting to 1. Verified live: swapping to Arachnus storm cannon on one arm and Iliastus accelerator culverin on the other now shows exactly those two weapons with no leftover caestus/projector, totals 517pts (367 + 90 + 60) correctly, and a third swap attempt is refused since only 2 arms exist. Found during the same investigation, NOT fixed here (needs its own pass — see ki-galatus-contemptor-infernus-incinerator-swap-01): the Galatus Contemptor Dreadnought has the identical \"each\"-worded swap group, but its 2 Infernus incinerators are conditionally granted by a different option group's choice rather than being in the base loadout, which the Telemon's fix does not account for.",
