    description: "FIXED 2026-08-27, reported on Discord (Liquid Citrus: \"it seems a henchman warband of more than one model wouldn't be allowed in Skirmish\"; Stu, same thread: \"I believe that's an issue with the app as they shouldn't have squadron from what I can see on the excel sheet\"). CAUSE: `validators.ts`'s Skirmish Squadron check (Missions.txt, \"units with the 'Squadron' rule may only field one model per slot\") scans each unit's `abilities` array for the literal word \"squadron\" — correct for the 97 units that genuinely print it there. Henchman Warband's own Inquisition.ods sheet has NO such text (only recruitment rules, plus \"All models form a single unit together and can't detach individually\" — incompatible with the vehicle-squadron premise); the word only appears in `henchman_warband.ts`'s abilities array because that list is a CONSTRUCTED summary of what each included specialist grants (\"Command Squad, Squadron: granted by Penitent/Sage/Exorcist/Mystic/Alien World Scout/Archaeotech Researcher/Crusader\"), copied from those specialists' own standalone Elite sheets (Penitents, Sages, Exorcists, Mystics, Alien World Scouts, Archaeotech Researchers, Crusaders), which DO genuinely print \"Squadron\" as their own ability. Scanning the Warband's derived summary text caught the word out of context and capped the whole 6-12-model unit at 1 model in Skirmish. FIX: excluded \"Henchman Warband\" by name from the abilities-text scan (the `is_squadron` flag and `unit_type` checks still apply and were never true for it either). Verified live: a 3-model Henchman Warband (2 Acolyte + 1 Penitent) in Skirmish shows no Squadron error; a standalone Penitents Elite squad at 2 models still correctly shows \"Skirmish: Penitents is a Squadron — maximum 1 model (have 2).\"",
