    description: "FIXED 2026-08-25, reported on Discord (rem, screenshot of Kill Team Veterans: \"i only put 1 gravis selection, 1 plasma pistol, 1 thunder hammer... here it says there's x5 of everything basically\"). CAUSE: `computeWeaponGroups` in `resolver.ts` already computes per-weapon `countOverrides` for two cases — a squad option-group swap (\"two Plague Marines may swap their Bolters\") and a promoted Champion's own Armory-bought gear (which gets its own `count: 1` group, split out earlier in the same function). A weapon bought individually from the Armory on a unit where several ORDINARY models can each buy their own item (no single Champion role — Kill Team Veterans, `has_armory_access: true` with `champion_has_armory: false`) fell into neither case: it isn't a squad-swap grant (`grantedQty`/`replacedQty` are built purely from `unit.option_groups` + `item.optionQty`, never from `item.armory`), and it isn't extracted into a Champion's own row (there is no Champion). It landed in the single unlabelled squad group with no override at all, so `WeaponTable`'s `countOverrides?.get(w.name) ?? count` fell back to the group's model count. Verified live: a 5-model Kill Team Veterans with one each of Bolt rifle/Plasma pistol/Thunder hammer bought from the Armory showed \"5x\" of each. FIX: added a branch alongside the existing multi-copy-base-loadout fallback — for a weapon that's Armory-granted (`grantedSet.has`) and not on the unit's own datasheet at all (`!datasheetNames.has`, so it can't be a dual-purpose squad-swap weapon already handled elsewhere), count the matching entries in `item.armory` (each selection is one model's purchase) and use that as the override. Verified live: the same unit now shows \"1x Bolt rifle\", \"1x Plasma pistol\", \"1x Thunder hammer\"; the base \"5x Frag grenade\"/\"5x Krak grenade\" rows are unaffected.",
