    description: "FOUND 2026-08-26 during the HH audit as a consistency oddity (all 8 non-Saturnine units shared `inline_pts: null` on this option group, differing from Saturnine's own `inline_pts: 2` — normalized Saturnine to match at first, treating the null pattern as the presumed-correct, consistent shape). Rigzar caught it live right after: \"legion heavy suport squad tiene una regla que dice... +1 point... creo que no esta implementada\" — confirming the 8-unit \"consistent\" pattern was itself the bug, not Saturnine's differently-shaped group. CAUSE: `points.ts`'s option-group pricing loop only adds `inline_pts` for an `__inline` toggle when `g.inline_pts` is truthy (`if (qty && g.inline_pts) total += g.inline_pts * (g.per_model ? item.size : 1)`) — with `inline_pts: null` the ability was silently free on every one of the 8 units (Legion Breacher/Tactical/Tactical Support/Terminator Cataphractii/Palatine Blade/Sky-hunter/Heavy Support/Kakophoni Squad), despite each one's own header stating a real per-model cost. FIX: set `inline_pts` to the header's own stated value (1 point on all 8; Saturnine's own +2 was already correct and left alone, just re-added after the earlier normalization had wrongly stripped it) and added `per_model: true` to all 9, matching the toggle-scaling pattern already used correctly elsewhere (e.g. the Astartes chainsword upgrade). Verified live: toggling it on a 5-model Legion Tactical Squad added exactly +5pts (205→210).",
