    description: "FIXED 2026-08-16 (v1.63), GitHub #90: \"Windriders — Twin shuriken catapults are completely removed as soon as I choose 1 alternate weapon.\" CAUSE: the per-weapon count override computes `(group count) x copies - swaps`, and a plain one-group squad carries a NULL group count, so the subtraction worked off ONE model: max(0, 1-1) = 0 and the weapon vanished for everyone. Confirmed NOT a v1.62 regression — the same result comes out of the previous release. SCOPE: 93 datasheets could be emptied this way, one Big choppa clearing every Ork Boy's Choppa among them. FIX: the group falls back to the unit's model count when it is the unlabelled whole-squad row (labelled rows always carry a real count, so a champion's row cannot be inflated). THREE MORE CAUSES surfaced from the leftovers, each read against its own sheet rather than assumed to be the same bug: (a) a loadout clause covering TWO model rows — \"Every Jakhal and Jakhal Pack Leader is equipped with:\", also Voidscarred and Kroot Farstalkers — left the group with no count, and a swap group scoped `applies_to_model: \"Jakhal\"` did not recognise that row as containing Jakhals; (b) `replaces` naming multi-profile rows one by one (\"Kroot rifle - Melee\", \"Kroot rifle - Ranged\") was looked up by base name and matched nothing — 9 datasheets; (c) the multi-copy arithmetic scaled the BASE instead of the cost of a swap, so four Penitent Engines read 3 flails after one swap instead of 6 and six Kastelan Robots read 5 Power fists instead of 10 — the datasheet says which (\"may swap BOTH Penitent flails\" removes two, \"may replace ONE Macro-scalpel\" removes one). Verified with a 2613-row before/after render of every unit including swap states; every changed row was classified and each class checked against canon.",
