    title: 'A squad showed the weapons of a special model it had not bought',
    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13, the general form of GitHub #87. Datasheets write a separate loadout sentence per model group — "Every Voidscarred and Felarch is equipped with: ...", then "A Shade Runner is equipped with: ...", and so on — and the engine matches those sentences to models by name so it can hide the weapons of a model with a count of zero. Production carried only the first sentence on twenty-one datasheets, so those weapons read as squad-wide kit. Nine were fixed here (Sisters Novitiate, Repentia Squad, Corsair Voidscarred with all three specialists, Atalan Jackals, Gretchins, Snotlings, Firesight Marksman, R\'varna and Y\'vahra Battlesuits); Guardian Defenders and Storm Guardians were done with #87. TWO ENGINE FIXES WERE NEEDED FOR THEM TO WORK AT ALL. First, the matcher only understood "Every <model> is equipped with"; the Voidscarred specialists read "A Shade Runner is equipped with", so their clauses were parsed by nothing — it now accepts Every / Each / A / An / The. Second, and caught only by testing the result: the specialists each carry a Plasma grenade and so does every Voidscarred and Felarch in the squad, so hiding the absent model\'s weapons stripped the grenade from ten models who have one. A weapon shared with a model that IS present now stays. DELIBERATELY NOT ADDED, and this corrects an earlier note of ours: the Exarch clauses on Dire Avengers, Fire Dragons, Shining Spears and Dark Reapers, and the Tauros Venator. Those models are `variant_models`, and the resolver identifies their weapons precisely BY THEIR ABSENCE from the loadout text (`variantOnlyWeapons`) — writing the clause in would make an Exarch\'s Diresword show on a squad with no Exarch. Verified that they already behave correctly. Eleven more clauses name a model production spells differently (the sheet\'s "Serpent shield platform" against its own model row\'s "Serpent scale platform", "Scarab Occult Sorceror", "Cult Standardbearer", the seven Cryptek specialisations) and are left alone.',
