    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13, GitHub #89: "The plattforms weapons are added to the Defenders instead of the platform itself, ending with 10 missile launchers and 10 star canons for the defenders." Reproduced exactly. TWO faults, both in `computeWeaponGroups`. (1) A weapon named in no loadout clause was dumped into groups[0] — the first model group — and a swapped-in weapon is by definition in no clause, so the Aeldari missile launcher landed on the Guardian Defender row and inherited its count. Weapons that can only arrive through an option group carrying `applies_to_model` are now routed to that model\'s group. (2) The hide-threshold for the replaced weapon used the whole squad size, so both platforms could trade their Scatter laser away and the laser stayed on the profile; a swap scoped to one model group is finished once THAT group\'s models have taken it. A THIRD fault surfaced while checking the rest of the game: production writes ammo variants with parentheses ("Bolt rifle (Bolt ammo)") while `baseName` only strips " - ", so an ammo-profile weapon never matched the choice that granted it and printed the model count instead of the quantity bought. Fixed as a fallback lookup rather than by normalising the keys, because `replaces` lists sometimes name profiles individually ("Kroot rifle - Melee", "Kroot rifle - Ranged") and collapsing those would double their quantity. MEASURED ACROSS THE GAME: 16 option groups are scoped to a named model group, and each was resolved and inspected rather than patched on shape — only Guardian Defenders and the Indomitus Crusader Squad actually misattributed. The others share a loadout clause with the model the swap targets (Voidscarred and Felarch, Farstalker and Kill-Broker), so one row is correct, and all of them already printed the right quantity. Regression net: 670 units × 1595 selection cases, zero exceptions.',
