    description: 'DONE 2026-08-13 with `scripts/ods_audit.cjs`, which reported 1,740 differences across the game. Most are modelling decisions rather than faults — Tyranid biomorphs, Eldar Exarch powers and Ork Kustom jobs are Armory sections that production models as per-unit option choices, and that alone accounts for over a thousand. What was real: seventeen Inquisition retinue datasheets capped at the Warband\'s 6 instead of their own limit; eight points corrections (Inquisition Land Raider Prometheus, Chimera and Taurox, and four option prices); four stat corrections (Chimera BS, Taurox Strength, Land Raider WS, Purestrain Genestealer Initiative); three unit sizes (Harlequin Troupe, Skyweavers, IG Heavy Weapon Squad); and the loadout clauses covered above. A BLIND SPOT IN THE TOOL WAS FOUND AND FIXED FIRST: it read each unit file by slicing the object literal out and running JSON.parse, which throws on any datasheet that references a TypeScript constant — every Tau unit with drones shares TAU_DRONE_CHOICES — so those files were skipped and the units reported as "NOT IN PRODUCTION". Twenty units across five factions, including every Tau Battlesuit, had never actually been audited. It now loads the faction\'s own units index through tsx. Deliberately not changed, all verified against their sheets: variant-model rows the audit reads as squad entries (CSM Sinister Bishop, Ork Pain Boss), and names where the sheet contradicts itself and production picked the consistent one (Grey Knights "Twin psycannon" for a weapon that only exists as "Twin heavy psycannon", Ork "Big shoota with Grot Gunner", Great Unclean One "Bile sword", Eldar "Star cannon").',
