    description: 'DONE 2026-08-13. Every faction sheet is now identical to the author\'s live Google Sheet, checked by `scripts/fetch_codex.cjs`; thirteen were behind. Two carried units nobody could build: the Necron Canoptek Tomb Stalker, and four Imperial Guard Elite advisors (Ambassador, Company Hero with its Animal Companion, Scribe Historicus, Staff Officer). Points and profiles that moved: Tervigon 237→223 with a reworked Stinger salvo, Tyrannofex 225→222, Canoptek Spyder claws S T→U, Dark Eldar Dracon redeploying two units, every Tyranid Lash whip and Bonesword gaining Deadly(5+), the Tyranid Prime and Warriors becoming Monstrous Infantry, a Neurothrope upgrade on the Zoanthrope Brood, and new melee options on both Guard command squads. TWO THINGS WORTH KNOWING FOR NEXT TIME. First, a delta shows what changed in the SHEET, not what is wrong with us: most of the Necron and Ork differences were already correct in production and the sheet was catching up — War scythe AP-4, Dynasty Scion 44, Reanimator 144, Lootas Rokkit launcha AP-3, the Technothrall→Cryptothrall rename. Second, the author is running a terminology sweep of his own: "invulnerability save" → "ward save" everywhere (which we did in v1.57), plus a steady stream of "cover" → "light cover" / "heavy cover" corrections — the Space Marine Stormcaller, the Ork \'Eavy armour cabin, the Harlequin Mirage launcher on three datasheets, and the Eldar Conceal and Reveal. Expect more of those. STILL OPEN: running `ods_audit.cjs` over a faction whose sheet barely moved surfaces a large PRE-EXISTING backlog, because it is the first field-by-field comparison these have had. Eldar alone reports 197 differences unrelated to any delta — missing second `equipped_with` clauses (the Guardian Defenders\' Heavy weapon platform, the Storm Guardians\' Serpent shield platform, several Exarchs), a missing Crimson Hunter Exarch model, and a Wraithlord option priced 0 against the sheet\'s 1. That backlog is not addressed here.',
