    id: 'ki-vehicles-general-armory-01',
    status: 'fixed',
    title: 'Every vehicle in the game was offered the infantry Armory',
    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13, raised by a player pushing back on an answer of ours. Checked against all 19 live sheets: 178 vehicle datasheets say "Has access to vehicle equipment from the Armory" and NOT ONE grants general access. The sheets say it structurally as well — the general WEAPON and EQUIPMENT sections are priced "POINTS / POINTS CHARACTER MODELS" with no vehicle column at all, while VEHICLE UPGRADES carries its own, and the note at the head of every Armory sheet reads "Items with a cost of \'-\' can not be selected". No price for your model type means you cannot take it. The app enforced that "-" rule for characters but had no notion of it for vehicles: `showArmory` admitted any vehicle so long as the faction had regular items ANYWHERE, so a Rhino was offered a power sword and a Predator a jump pack, at the normal-model price. 188 vehicles across 17 factions were affected. Now a non-character vehicle sees only the vehicle section, both in the button (UnitCard) and in the item list (ArmoryModal `filterByUnitType`, alongside the existing Tau-infantry rule). THE ONE EXCEPTION, and the reason this was not a one-liner: Ork Kustom jobs. They are their own section on the sheet, flat-priced rather than per hull point, and 13 Ork vehicle datasheets explicitly say "Can get one Kustom job" — so Ork vehicles keep exactly those 16 items and nothing else. Verified across every faction: only Orks report a non-zero count. Character-bodied vehicles keep full access, since their relics are priced via p_char. The engine\'s grant path is untouched — vehicle upgrades that hand over a weapon (Hunter-killer missile, Storm bolter, Heavy stubber, Twin heavy stubber, Stikkbombz launcha) are vehicle-category equipment whose weapon profile is looked up in armory_general.weapons directly, not through the UI.',
