    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13, found while checking the vehicle Armory rule above. Two canon limits were unenforced. (1) "Every Kustom job is unique." The Orks Armory prints that ONCE at the foot of the KUSTOM JOBS section instead of on each of the sixteen entries, so `isUniqueItem(arm.desc)` never saw it and the same Kustom job could be bought by every unit in the army. (2) "Can get one Kustom job." The per-unit limit was not enforced at all: each job is a different item, so none of them ever tripped the per-item cap and a single Trukk could buy all sixteen. Both now enforced in `isAddBlocked`. The Waaagh! Coast Kustoms trait is deliberately left alone — it raises the per-ITEM cap ("each Kustom job can be taken one additional time"), it does not give a unit a second job. NOT modelled as a new armoury category: the AdMech Doctrina pattern (category \'veteran\') was the obvious reuse and is wrong here, because veteran items are priced per Wound or Hull point while Kustom jobs are flat, so it would have mis-priced all sixteen. Each job\'s own restriction ("Vehicle only", "Warbuggy only", "Battlewagon and Battle Fortress only", "Mek and Big Mek only", "Walker only", "Spanna only", "Transport vehicle only", "Non-walker or aircraft vehicle only") is shown in its description but is still not enforced by the engine — a player has to read it. Also corrected from the sheet: \'Eavy armour cabin grants LIGHT cover, not cover.',
