    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13. The author\'s answer to a question we raised on the Flamestorm cannon: "the Storm bolter swap can be done if you select a weapon that comes with one." The Dreadnought\'s default loadout is "-", and only two of the twelve entries in "Must pick two weapons from this list" carry a Storm bolter (the Dreadnought claw and the Dreadnought close combat weapon). The "Can swap a Storm bolter" group was offered unconditionally, so a Dreadnought armed with, say, a Twin lascannon and a Multi-melta could still buy a Heavy flamer "in exchange for" a Storm bolter it never had. New `OptionGroup.requires_choice`: the group is hidden until a choice that grants the weapon is selected, and the validator rejects the selection on a list imported with it already in place. DELIBERATELY NOT DERIVED FROM `replaces`, which was the obvious general rule and is wrong: measured across the game, 19 groups replace a weapon absent from `equipped_with`, and 16 of those are a Champion\'s or Exarch\'s own gear that the base loadout sentence never mentions (Eldar Exarchs, the Voidscarred Felarch, and so on — the resolver has `variantOnlyWeapons` for exactly this). A blanket gate would have hidden all sixteen. Verified in the browser: with the Dreadnought claw selected the swap group is there, and it disappears the moment the claw is deselected.',
