    title: 'Adeptus Mechanicus — Bionics became wargear, and default-loadout gear now applies its rule',
    description: 'FIXED 2026-08-13 with the August codex. The author stopped printing "Bionics: The model receives a 6+ ward save." as an ability on fifteen datasheets and instead lists Bionics in the model\'s equipped-with line, expecting the reader to look it up in the Armory (where it already sat at 3/9 pts). The engine only ever resolved WEAPONS out of that sentence, so copying the sheet verbatim would have silently deleted the ward save from every Skitarii, Kataphron, Sicaran, Pteraxii, Serberys, Sydonian and Ironstrider unit in the codex. FIX: `resolveUnitProfile` now also matches equipment names in `equipped_with` against the reachable armouries and feeds them through the same `parseEquipMods` path as bought items. Three exclusions, each measured across all 19 factions first: items with an `armourKeyword` (armour is modelled by the unit\'s own keyword and would double-count the statline bonuses — Gravis armor on four Space Marine squads); names that are also a weapon on that datasheet (several armouries list a weapon in the equipment section too — the IG Heavy stubber on five vehicles, Dark Eldar Bladevanes, the Tyranid Acid Maw, the Judicar\'s Relic blade); and names under three characters, because "-" is a real entry in some equipment tables. CRITICAL SECOND HALF, caught in verification: default gear contributes only its RULE TEXT and its ward save, never stat deltas or armour saves. A datasheet\'s printed statline is authored with the default loadout already on the model — a Space Marine Assault Squad prints 12" precisely BECAUSE every model carries a Jump pack — so applying the item\'s "+6\\" movement" on top would have moved them to 18". Ward saves are the exception worth carrying because they appear in no stat column, which is exactly why Bionics has to come from here. Verified: Skitarii Rangers keep a 6+ ward with no Bionics ability line, and the Assault Squad keeps its printed 12" while gaining the Jump pack rule text.',
